interpretation:
AVF v0.2 consumes Local DRS v0.2 advisory/reuse/risk signals and produces candidate pressure, hard masks, soft penalties, score explanations, and a ranked advisory report.

AVF v0.2 has the right to say where to look.
AVF v0.2 has the right to say where not to go.
AVF v0.2 does not have the right to say that action is allowed.
AVF v0.2 does not decide.
AVF v0.2 does not grant permission.
AVF v0.2 does not create truth.
AVF v0.2 does not create FinalOutput.
AVF v0.2 does not create ActionCommitPacket.
AVF v0.2 does not create receipt.
AVF v0.2 does not execute payment.
AVF v0.2 does not release shipment.
AVF v0.2 cannot bypass Root.

Root remains final authority.

audit_conclusion:
AVF v0.2 after Local DRS v0.2 closure is PASS for local candidate/risk model, deterministic evaluator/advisory ranking, deterministic Full WOW v1.2 product trace integration, and adversarial hard-mask/non-authority hardening. The audited layer remains advisory, local, deterministic, and effect-free.
